<!-- formalization -->

**Definition (`InfoSys.liftLeft`).** The left lift of a finite set $v \subseteq D_{\mathbf{A}}$ is the finite set of left-injection tokens $(x, \Delta_{\mathbf{B}})$ for $x \in v$.

**Theorem (`InfoSys.liftLeft.mem_foldr`).** Membership in a left lift built by folding insertion over a multiset equals membership of some left injection over that multiset.

*Proof.* Induction on the multiset, using the characterization of insert membership. □

**Theorem (`InfoSys.liftLeft.mem`).** A token lies in the left lift of $v$ iff it is a left injection of some $x \in v$.

*Proof.* Unfold the lift and apply the fold characterization. □

**Theorem (`InfoSys.liftLeft.fstFinset_eq`).** The first projection of a left lift is the original set $v$.

*Proof.* Use membership characterizations of first projection and of the lift. □

**Theorem (`InfoSys.liftLeft.sndFinset_eq`).** The second projection of a left lift is contained in $\{\Delta_{\mathbf{B}}\}$.

*Proof.* Each token in the lift has second component $\Delta_{\mathbf{B}}$. □

**Theorem (`InfoSys.liftLeft.con`).** The left lift of a consistent set $v$ is consistent in the product system.

*Proof.* First projection recovers $v$; second projection lies in the singleton of bottom. □
